type
Usage: type NAME...

Shell builtin. Say what NAME actually is: a builtin, a function, an
alias, or a path to a program. Useful when a command does not behave the
way the manual for the program says -- often because it is a builtin and
never reached the program at all.

	type cd		cd is a shell builtin
	type ls		ls is /bin/ls

See also: which, hash
